# Golden emitted-text assets are byte-exact contracts (mod.ini/hlsl = LF, *.json = CRLF, as the
# emitter writes them). No EOL conversion — an autocrlf rewrite on checkout would silently break
# the byte-for-byte golden comparison.
tests/Remold.Core.Tests/Migoto/golden/** -text

# The pinned Build/project fixtures are the same kind of contract, and one of them
# (legacy_build_v1.json) is compared as text against a freshly serialized snapshot. Its committed
# bytes are LF, and the snapshot is written with an LF newline on every platform, so the comparison
# no longer answers to whatever core.autocrlf a checkout was made under.
tests/Remold.Core.Tests/Project/golden/*.json -text
